    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green: **255 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `membershipTier` field is a computed, read-only field on the owner response, so I followed the same pattern the codebase already uses for `displayName`, `initials`, and `membershipNumber`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `membershipTier` (string, read-only) property to the `Owner` schema. `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time, so this produces the getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct expression mapping `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(membershipTier(owner))\")` plus a `membershipTier(Owner)` default method implementing the rule:\n   ```java\n   return (namesakeCount == 0 && email present) ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n   ```\n   Email is treated as present when non-null and non-blank; a null `namesakeCount` falls through to `BRONZE`.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass, and no existing tests regressed.",
